{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01NsRreqCtRoebirMGRGA15s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q14: Detect and stop infinite planning loops?**\n\n---\n\n**Key content in `answers/03-014-detect-and-stop-infinite-planning-loops.md`:**\n\n**Core concept:** The LLM cannot reliably detect its own loops — loop control must be enforced in the **orchestrator code**, not the prompt.\n\n**Four-signal detection stack:**\n1. **Hard step cap** — `if steps >= MAX_STEPS: raise BudgetExceededError` — catches any loop, guaranteed\n2. **Wall-clock timeout** — `asyncio.wait_for(agent_loop(), timeout=120s)` — catches slow cycles and network hangs\n3. **No-progress detector** — MD5 fingerprint of `(tool_name, canonicalized_args)` per step; if last 3 hashes are identical → stuck (the signal candidates always miss)\n4. **Token budget cap** — cumulative token counter halts the loop before cost explosion\n\n**Plus:** a re-planning counter for the subtle *goal-drift* variant where the LLM keeps generating new sub-plans with no tool calls — after 3 consecutive thought-only steps, force an action or escalate to HITL.\n\n**Key pitfall called out:** Saying \"I'd add a note in the system prompt to stop if looping\" — prompts can't enforce hard limits; the orchestrator must own termination.\n\n**Calibration rule:** Set `MAX_STEPS = expected_steps × 3`, trigger async HITL at `× 2`, and always checkpoint state before raising the budget exception so the human reviewer has full context."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":281,"cache_read_input_tokens":67063,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":281,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5dc1e79f-67c8-4688-96d1-75fbd0cd9a0c","uuid":"0d549732-05bf-4284-a46f-766ee474f9a9"}
